cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use lptlib in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "lptlib: A parallel Lagrangian particle tracking library for compressible CFD data and tracer-response analysis in optical velocimetry"
abstract: >-
  lptlib is a Python library for one-way coupled Lagrangian particle tracking in
  steady and unsteady compressible CFD data. It reads structured, multi-block,
  curvilinear PLOT3D grid and flow fields, locates arbitrary points inside the
  curvilinear domain, interpolates the flow state to those points, and integrates
  fluid streamlines and inertial particle trajectories through the field under a
  selectable spherical-particle drag closure. Large ensembles run in parallel
  through multiprocessing, thread pools, or MPI, with adaptive time stepping for
  the stiff dynamics near shocks, and scattered tracks can be reduced back onto a
  structured mesh to produce PIV-like Eulerian fields.
type: software
